[{:db/id "q-83401/selection/b336641abcb999c21c9e53c96c83b284fdf2bf3a3de0d87fa53f648928975e27" :answer/id #uuid "83461d3b-e6d9-54bd-aeb2-2fc4b0ba255c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83401/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "cd06b297-72a6-58de-ac7a-3d9ada651f35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83401/selection/ee875d10153fa4bb909fbbc627a25a7be015bf21281d6aad66ce58387afa62eb" :answer/id #uuid "bfce075a-c691-59ca-af67-f0cd241ec419" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83401/selection/33e717c85134a1af4a888dacae2baa68b87f940d55222cf7821885d0a9b49e91" :answer/id #uuid "96e2c389-0303-5d1d-9e14-5df830b874aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83401/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "0fa5d8ef-02ae-5024-bfe1-202aee9190bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83401/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "865089c0-2f55-5735-913e-196d4b70d3a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83401/selection/33e717c85134a1af4a888dacae2baa68b87f940d55222cf7821885d0a9b49e91" :answer-field/choices ["q-83401/selection/b336641abcb999c21c9e53c96c83b284fdf2bf3a3de0d87fa53f648928975e27" "q-83401/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-83401/selection/ee875d10153fa4bb909fbbc627a25a7be015bf21281d6aad66ce58387afa62eb" "q-83401/selection/33e717c85134a1af4a888dacae2baa68b87f940d55222cf7821885d0a9b49e91" "q-83401/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83401" :question/id #uuid "ea9eaa52-b07b-579c-b027-1db28f380c68" :question/math-academy-id "q-83401" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,2t⟩$ for $t\\ge 0$, use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(1,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,0,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨{e}^{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,2t⟩ & =⟨1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}=1 \\\\ {t}^{3}=0 \\\\ 2t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=0.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(1,0,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨1,0,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,6t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =2j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\sqrt{5})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83401/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eddc00c0-eac2-5e79-84be-b90cc27eb054"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131970/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7a21af80-abba-5c34-84e9-adc272087d88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131970/selection/9626d65a8e62ab849e2d04722e514be58f991944ca113d732e76abff54736378" :answer/id #uuid "c154d580-626e-507f-a824-19c52ccccd9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131970/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "4e638470-8ce9-5e9d-af2f-747328c49416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131970/selection/8a008595dbd9de87f0f7b53d7ce22b40a994912291fe2a6ce241519d4271f52e" :answer/id #uuid "14967e8b-2741-542b-9821-eeab3806648f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131970/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "333c13fd-c3bd-5dac-97ae-a5a4fbb9e10f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131970/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f38f90d-3b12-52a6-9ad1-4e6db97597eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131970/selection/9626d65a8e62ab849e2d04722e514be58f991944ca113d732e76abff54736378" :answer-field/choices ["q-131970/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-131970/selection/9626d65a8e62ab849e2d04722e514be58f991944ca113d732e76abff54736378" "q-131970/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-131970/selection/8a008595dbd9de87f0f7b53d7ce22b40a994912291fe2a6ce241519d4271f52e" "q-131970/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131970" :question/id #uuid "64fc2a14-fee2-5335-8823-e0d8cf577911" :question/math-academy-id "q-131970" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,t⟩$ for $t\\ge 0,$ use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(1,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,0,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,t⟩ & =⟨1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=1 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=0 \\\\ t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, $t=0.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(1,0,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{e}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-{e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨-2{e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,-2{e}^{-0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,0⟩⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-2i-2k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+0+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131970/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eddc00c0-eac2-5e79-84be-b90cc27eb054"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131970"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83402/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer/id #uuid "ef3d9bab-704b-5baa-9890-c3dfd09a2f47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83402/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" :answer/id #uuid "a117f076-775d-5747-a5cd-6f842baa977a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83402/selection/9628302a1ca469d39232d6a3b6b23e1bb9ffabf13ad87df8534f1e55d7195c04" :answer/id #uuid "055afff6-82e4-52d8-bc90-e7a97c956b65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83402/selection/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980" :answer/id #uuid "a400555e-21a3-5c83-a2b3-7f3a99baccdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83402/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "e9f6a2f0-4cbc-589a-9d93-f89626128665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83402/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ebd2a1b-13cc-5ba4-a03c-4c4816f6a261" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83402/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer-field/choices ["q-83402/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" "q-83402/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5395e9d793e225144a0384a1ba" "q-83402/selection/9628302a1ca469d39232d6a3b6b23e1bb9ffabf13ad87df8534f1e55d7195c04" "q-83402/selection/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980" "q-83402/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83402" :question/id #uuid "36e34b5e-9c3c-5c2f-91a2-6dd8d8382f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-83402" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩$ for $t>0$, use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(2,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩ & =⟨2,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(2,1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(1),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨2,2,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(1) & =⟨0,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-4i+2j+4k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+16} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(1){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{3}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83402/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eddc00c0-eac2-5e79-84be-b90cc27eb054"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131968/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "29fd0d04-e4ea-5d71-8f46-446e91c2e6b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131968/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "a9f80daa-4180-5dba-a7c1-33c60608f102" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131968/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "75b51958-c1eb-5e61-95e3-e0f98dfc81e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131968/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e4ba86bc-7907-576d-9fef-c98ae4c8972b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131968/selection/c8e05ee3041954783cf5e95ad263b9c8b435f3ec61da70c23934bf1f912ef447" :answer/id #uuid "402009ae-2d6d-5b28-bb8d-3e5ad61e5c91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131968/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0282fe1-1422-51b7-b372-3e4d4328ba2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131968/selection/c8e05ee3041954783cf5e95ad263b9c8b435f3ec61da70c23934bf1f912ef447" :answer-field/choices ["q-131968/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-131968/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-131968/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-131968/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-131968/selection/c8e05ee3041954783cf5e95ad263b9c8b435f3ec61da70c23934bf1f912ef447"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131968" :question/id #uuid "0556bd30-af31-5596-a2e3-09c389614b69" :question/math-academy-id "q-131968" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,2t⟩$ for $t\\ge 0,$ use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(1,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,1,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,2t⟩ & =⟨1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}=1 \\\\ {e}^{-t}=1 \\\\ 2t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, $t=0.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(1,1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{e}^{0},-{e}^{-0},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨{e}^{0},{e}^{-0},0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-2i+2j+2k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{6\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131968/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eddc00c0-eac2-5e79-84be-b90cc27eb054"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131968"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131959/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "da71a241-5820-5b41-8770-95e613e06e7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131959/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "6d90cfb2-b731-5eae-b023-971f0457ace7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131959/selection/5bd506083b26258fa0a95592fb35bf47cdd382f7f42161f0c65d3072d0e5167a" :answer/id #uuid "ba2da6db-bd61-57eb-b670-5d089274ab2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131959/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "95498863-d2c4-5a40-9649-e023ccb4bca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131959/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer/id #uuid "c3851783-37ff-5d63-83af-edc1363edc16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131959/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b52ee70-6a45-59a8-a321-86ffdfd82696" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131959/selection/5bd506083b26258fa0a95592fb35bf47cdd382f7f42161f0c65d3072d0e5167a" :answer-field/choices ["q-131959/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-131959/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-131959/selection/5bd506083b26258fa0a95592fb35bf47cdd382f7f42161f0c65d3072d0e5167a" "q-131959/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-131959/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131959" :question/id #uuid "17a0543f-34f5-5c67-8971-3c0e51750b04" :question/math-academy-id "q-131959" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4t⟩$ for $0\\le t<2\\pi ,$ use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(0,-3,4\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(0,-3,4\\pi )$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0,-3,4\\pi ⟩ \\\\ ⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4t⟩ & =⟨0,-3,4\\pi ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-3 \\\\ 4t=4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, $t=\\pi .$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(0,-3,4\\pi )$ is at the tip of $r(\\pi ).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,4⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-12i-9k \\\\  & =3(-4i-3k) \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =3\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =3(5) \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{{5}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131959/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eddc00c0-eac2-5e79-84be-b90cc27eb054"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131959"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165244/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "0d4cbc2e-9d33-5798-a347-3ddd07980b9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165244/selection/eb06e2b413bd20e6333e7fa62e3f3011d7c93838f703e47415d67086fae753b9" :answer/id #uuid "d232be54-1563-5e82-b841-0e4a733b29eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165244/selection/48636a7405f69204b02a78e6bd1a930b3e014b5ed89a13b2c10bfcc1da9cf380" :answer/id #uuid "fe228705-a15f-5bab-b95e-033544aaf9ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165244/selection/8e505bf5b7fdf032ce802be7bb5a088b4ca0699eb8148a652128b43ed89707db" :answer/id #uuid "9b45df3c-d62b-5fd7-bdd5-734b80993078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165244/selection/4c30092f1e87bb04bef002e0c2e618824d1dbfdd00ae6d4d58b4d466ba37f2f9" :answer/id #uuid "c38538d5-d651-51ff-a392-e5df4c4d4a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{t}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165244/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7460673c-2d72-5d62-ac67-5a952dfd384b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-165244/selection/8e505bf5b7fdf032ce802be7bb5a088b4ca0699eb8148a652128b43ed89707db" :answer-field/choices ["q-165244/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-165244/selection/eb06e2b413bd20e6333e7fa62e3f3011d7c93838f703e47415d67086fae753b9" "q-165244/selection/48636a7405f69204b02a78e6bd1a930b3e014b5ed89a13b2c10bfcc1da9cf380" "q-165244/selection/8e505bf5b7fdf032ce802be7bb5a088b4ca0699eb8148a652128b43ed89707db" "q-165244/selection/4c30092f1e87bb04bef002e0c2e618824d1dbfdd00ae6d4d58b4d466ba37f2f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165244" :question/id #uuid "fc6695d3-06a1-5f96-b0f7-737ffb144ac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-165244" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{t}^{2},\\,t⟩,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature of this curve as a function of $t.$ \n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that* ${r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=-\\sqrt{2}\\,i+2t\\,j-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}t)}^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${t}^{2}+1>0$ for any real value $t.$\n\nSince we are told that\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=-\\sqrt{2}\\,i+2t\\,j-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}\\,k,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+4{t}^{2}+2{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{{({t}^{2}+1)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-165244/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b61ddc7-b781-5a25-b499-1ea6f48abf36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165244"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83439/selection/cf342c72b0cabe285200beee27d648936f701ff8506d8ae5c986eb1412d817c8" :answer/id #uuid "4f80c751-1b9c-54fb-b67e-702cd3878c4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83439/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "fd8dd439-a0ac-57a6-b6b8-c5c4b31cf7ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83439/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" :answer/id #uuid "80d69cde-422c-5a5b-9d14-f05f4df9dccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83439/selection/e52baf6f58a50be3f0aad1fe30f8b37e477346a1c9e6ca8a0db6be64cfef2da7" :answer/id #uuid "3c0dbd08-ed1d-5b81-98d4-4c7ab696c421" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83439/selection/645d28d457ec9bdcc4cf0d41f0530b2789529bbedd1a4070523983008b788ce5" :answer/id #uuid "7246e363-ff25-566e-b86a-571c7c94a623" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83439/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "933a210b-69c7-500d-b43f-79703540fcc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83439/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-83439/selection/cf342c72b0cabe285200beee27d648936f701ff8506d8ae5c986eb1412d817c8" "q-83439/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-83439/selection/c24232afb9b5ba9c1cc5619273d09a5676ecc0aa44d228853ae38c1edcbf08e1" "q-83439/selection/e52baf6f58a50be3f0aad1fe30f8b37e477346a1c9e6ca8a0db6be64cfef2da7" "q-83439/selection/645d28d457ec9bdcc4cf0d41f0530b2789529bbedd1a4070523983008b788ce5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83439" :question/id #uuid "bd9cfa87-7dff-5a04-a405-35501e7125bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-83439" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the second derivative ${r}^{″}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\times ⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}i-\\sqrt{2}j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the magnitude of the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(-\\sqrt{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2+2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{2}{(\\sqrt{2})^{3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-83439/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b61ddc7-b781-5a25-b499-1ea6f48abf36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83439"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86799/selection/99044035a59fe7f7bb673934c3abcbf76644e7625ba0d776e76905e9639ec970" :answer/id #uuid "1d9de9f0-1f45-50a7-a7f1-9379aaff10d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86799/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "62b12cce-be61-514e-989b-c0fe8d17d9dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86799/selection/e8d71736bf629f65cfe24280bf53c05df7407ffbab475b85b13adf8cd8619323" :answer/id #uuid "2a6962a4-edef-5657-82f7-e0d0ed2a42bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{(1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t))^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86799/selection/303bd508652417d2619d4d65da217e7eaef9da0481c6826bc1568013e578b130" :answer/id #uuid "b70b624f-4e86-53f1-871d-5db6b744ee99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{(1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t))^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86799/selection/adb16c0ae6d63ece7f135f15ec0dbc29456e8f3236e2bf50fdd1789f1dd37ea0" :answer/id #uuid "14b70082-d898-5772-ba41-00c5572a75f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86799/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0eb7d9c3-e2f2-5e38-8f8d-32510fd8d2ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86799/selection/e8d71736bf629f65cfe24280bf53c05df7407ffbab475b85b13adf8cd8619323" :answer-field/choices ["q-86799/selection/99044035a59fe7f7bb673934c3abcbf76644e7625ba0d776e76905e9639ec970" "q-86799/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-86799/selection/e8d71736bf629f65cfe24280bf53c05df7407ffbab475b85b13adf8cd8619323" "q-86799/selection/303bd508652417d2619d4d65da217e7eaef9da0481c6826bc1568013e578b130" "q-86799/selection/adb16c0ae6d63ece7f135f15ec0dbc29456e8f3236e2bf50fdd1789f1dd37ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86799" :question/id #uuid "04ab73dc-e7b5-5ca6-9a3f-c828499c1554" :question/math-academy-id "q-86799" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨-t,\\,4,\\,1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\pi $, use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the second derivative ${r}^{″}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩=⟨0,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the cross-product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨-1,0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\times ⟨0,0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the magnitude of the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =|\\operatorname{sin}⁡t|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\ge 0$ when $0\\le t\\le \\pi .$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{(1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t))^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86799/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b61ddc7-b781-5a25-b499-1ea6f48abf36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165242/selection/6929c14b9efc429003a0ba99f79a392867f34da73d9b0b59c6de4bd53c2a158c" :answer/id #uuid "f48e1755-003b-5005-a01e-e9125f99bf0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165242/selection/8c905d551f711f1a6b9b9eddc2d151b33bdb4c9d2966cfd4e115b133465127cd" :answer/id #uuid "07b92213-8180-59d7-bbb7-11a54407e889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165242/selection/abace1945516ae1bc9abe3886c42fcf2d24d217027c5746b9e617e2c21d9b779" :answer/id #uuid "4a081ba5-cdec-5033-bfc8-6ddcd73394f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(5{t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165242/selection/5a6cd9bd297c19fe0fd8171d685539acb691d28aa6b06ae3c9d64f7b366bfde2" :answer/id #uuid "ab4f07c4-6a4f-5760-944f-42f0496cb0b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(5{t}^{2}+1)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165242/selection/e30a7d6ff9f564b23f62f2e37780812a217b60f290a721ab375163cc8741f7b8" :answer/id #uuid "504fdf52-a521-592a-b704-e51121413bf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2(5{t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165242/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79328c8c-0883-5f8e-8cd0-b2d1d76aa674" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-165242/selection/e30a7d6ff9f564b23f62f2e37780812a217b60f290a721ab375163cc8741f7b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-165242/selection/6929c14b9efc429003a0ba99f79a392867f34da73d9b0b59c6de4bd53c2a158c" "q-165242/selection/8c905d551f711f1a6b9b9eddc2d151b33bdb4c9d2966cfd4e115b133465127cd" "q-165242/selection/abace1945516ae1bc9abe3886c42fcf2d24d217027c5746b9e617e2c21d9b779" "q-165242/selection/5a6cd9bd297c19fe0fd8171d685539acb691d28aa6b06ae3c9d64f7b366bfde2" "q-165242/selection/e30a7d6ff9f564b23f62f2e37780812a217b60f290a721ab375163cc8741f7b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165242" :question/id #uuid "da86715d-8126-5962-aa89-fa51c40c78dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-165242" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature of this curve as a function of $t.$ \n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=-8\\,i+4\\,j.$*" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,4t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2t)}^{2}+{(4t)}^{2}+{(2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4(5{t}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are told that\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=-8\\,i+4\\,j,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{(2\\sqrt{5{t}^{2}+1})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{8\\sqrt{(5{t}^{2}+1)^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2(5{t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-165242/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b61ddc7-b781-5a25-b499-1ea6f48abf36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165242"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86785/selection/c0715a2e7c728f82dc9410ef1e89eb7df1783bc83148d968aaaa28185d50feb3" :answer/id #uuid "97c36ceb-e02d-5b19-b92a-2847538913c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3t}{4(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86785/selection/4c5474464ccfe22e64aa5e85ea2d4c8cc61e9f1b0d976dfa88895a4c897ef95c" :answer/id #uuid "7f016fca-d7a4-5cf3-9a3d-4e2c9bd8be1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86785/selection/39084e3fa8aa6a7dc705d82bac710a5428945a32f451a9a3854c2aed8abd6a4c" :answer/id #uuid "80266bb2-9d25-548c-9741-94de26e98805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86785/selection/9e3d6a1deb73ae204d0f353a73b9519b47024d63f6b120dd39ca6669692ccb4f" :answer/id #uuid "38060121-0bf1-5af1-a15e-71cbd58dcaa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86785/selection/a33839a7c6e210e9f0972599b326f694f77416ebecb3d3e2c23f86bd9e7ee109" :answer/id #uuid "7a79e1c0-3fb0-5ec7-a381-8095f28d65c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{3(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86785/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "027cb776-8049-57af-9ac8-33a225c351f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86785/selection/a33839a7c6e210e9f0972599b326f694f77416ebecb3d3e2c23f86bd9e7ee109" :answer-field/choices ["q-86785/selection/c0715a2e7c728f82dc9410ef1e89eb7df1783bc83148d968aaaa28185d50feb3" "q-86785/selection/4c5474464ccfe22e64aa5e85ea2d4c8cc61e9f1b0d976dfa88895a4c897ef95c" "q-86785/selection/39084e3fa8aa6a7dc705d82bac710a5428945a32f451a9a3854c2aed8abd6a4c" "q-86785/selection/9e3d6a1deb73ae204d0f353a73b9519b47024d63f6b120dd39ca6669692ccb4f" "q-86785/selection/a33839a7c6e210e9f0972599b326f694f77416ebecb3d3e2c23f86bd9e7ee109"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86785" :question/id #uuid "08daaac0-fbd4-5500-8a88-44cc20910ea2" :question/math-academy-id "q-86785" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨3,\\,3t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩$ for $t>0,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩=⟨0,\\,3,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(3)^{2}+(3{t}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9(1+{t}^{4})} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the second derivative ${r}^{″}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩=⟨0,\\,0,\\,6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the cross-product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨0,\\,3,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,0,\\,6t⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 6t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 6t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =18t\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the magnitude of the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =|18t|=18t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $t>0$, we have $|t|=t.$\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{18t}{{(3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}})}^{3}}=\\frac{2t}{3(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-86785/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b61ddc7-b781-5a25-b499-1ea6f48abf36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86785"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86800/selection/b516bedaca31fbd0ea4981ce0c0e294dfa0e6f89c5606f74a3d5179610416504" :answer/id #uuid "2c03cbcb-7002-5e12-a5a0-6301c6593e52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86800/selection/68dfaffba3fe7660e4fe7f6db9287b4c036f0fb2a1e928c269ae62a88dea21c1" :answer/id #uuid "61910a38-c809-5331-a61d-4006120d4a01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{27(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86800/selection/53da88fd955232fcffca8b25d9a2b40a5fa8f64dfc5c78e394c8c4459f77949c" :answer/id #uuid "eaaf97ed-d317-5fa1-97e2-d5e9fe88e466" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86800/selection/2314250aa2bfa9d7aa73698aec3667c39f44fe8bc5e692260ffe475d0e90e809" :answer/id #uuid "cf4ec583-e157-5fb7-9366-299b67a611ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{9(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86800/selection/a33839a7c6e210e9f0972599b326f694f77416ebecb3d3e2c23f86bd9e7ee109" :answer/id #uuid "e9992417-8e8b-5a75-874f-3519067c1c3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2t}{3(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86800/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f665fad-ce17-5821-b8e1-2f7882ffd131" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86800/selection/a33839a7c6e210e9f0972599b326f694f77416ebecb3d3e2c23f86bd9e7ee109" :answer-field/choices ["q-86800/selection/b516bedaca31fbd0ea4981ce0c0e294dfa0e6f89c5606f74a3d5179610416504" "q-86800/selection/68dfaffba3fe7660e4fe7f6db9287b4c036f0fb2a1e928c269ae62a88dea21c1" "q-86800/selection/53da88fd955232fcffca8b25d9a2b40a5fa8f64dfc5c78e394c8c4459f77949c" "q-86800/selection/2314250aa2bfa9d7aa73698aec3667c39f44fe8bc5e692260ffe475d0e90e809" "q-86800/selection/a33839a7c6e210e9f0972599b326f694f77416ebecb3d3e2c23f86bd9e7ee109"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86800" :question/id #uuid "20720610-3b29-5e15-904f-53aa6331528d" :question/math-academy-id "q-86800" :question/problem "What is the curvature of the curve $r(t)=⟨3t,1-{t}^{3}⟩$, for $t>0?$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{3})⟩=⟨3,-3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-3{t}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{2})⟩=⟨0,-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨3,\\,-3{t}^{2},\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-6t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -3{t}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3{t}^{2} \\\\ 0 & -6t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-18t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=|-18t|=18t.\n$$\n\nNotice that since $t>0$, we have $|t|=t.$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18t}{(3\\sqrt{1+{t}^{4}})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18t}{27(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{3(1+{t}^{4})^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-86800/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca07aabe-9fdd-5f28-b39f-1971c3591f86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86800"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64761/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "af6bd89b-aef9-5651-98b9-18a06731d916" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64761/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "ac243059-1ee1-51a0-a5b5-3642096abd8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64761/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "d598d2b6-445b-51a3-afcd-c6db6a5ea2ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64761/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f6a1cb31-4691-54f2-bd28-26dc11691a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64761/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "1e238e7f-e27b-555a-96be-1329f9bd0234" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64761/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e82bdf8a-aea0-5e30-9a74-cf499c8dcf1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64761/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-64761/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-64761/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-64761/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-64761/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-64761/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64761" :question/id #uuid "42e675d7-c153-56a4-a60e-5f69b95ab1fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-64761" :question/problem "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}},\\,{e}^{t}⟩$ at the point where $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}},\\,{e}^{t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨-\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{1-{0}^{2}}},\\,{e}^{0}⟩=⟨0,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{(1-{t}^{2})}^{3/2}},\\,{e}^{t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(1-{0}^{2})^{3/2}},\\,{e}^{0}⟩=⟨-1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(0)$ and ${r}^{″}(0)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨0,\\,1,0⟩\\times ⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{(1)^{3}}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64761/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca07aabe-9fdd-5f28-b39f-1971c3591f86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64761"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34381/selection/b06cbb25313ebba12f59ebfc0e0cee6a6f5103f0607de43b037ce874e0096f5d" :answer/id #uuid "bda5e74e-d083-56ce-9dc3-328b12f7771f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6t}{(4+9{t}^{2})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34381/selection/0606c6f872a15cbcd8483d92c48658e5ff65191398a20929bb976b05389a3be5" :answer/id #uuid "55dfb07c-371c-5bb0-9c93-947330cfd3e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{t(4+9{t}^{2})^{1/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34381/selection/eb7fdef173dcb29d0b64e26e7f4a0ccc2896fd053835d1349f6a047afc188505" :answer/id #uuid "ea585fbf-a997-58e2-8e9b-ea9ed0591556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6{t}^{2}}{(4+9{t}^{2})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34381/selection/bbdb8bf102d7eb5d16d4f748a0670b7a73e5929c450674da840e0cb6c21eaae8" :answer/id #uuid "0f7033fe-8d58-5a00-b91d-dab9a8f9a307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{t(4+9{t}^{2})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34381/selection/90622d15656212878faedabd373eccc5d61aa366798c9308a65b9883426dc53e" :answer/id #uuid "863fe0d9-93d3-5b7b-9011-f90f4b7fcc85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{t(4+9{t}^{2})^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34381/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "064cad32-5831-57e8-ba64-ffbeb303b597" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34381/selection/bbdb8bf102d7eb5d16d4f748a0670b7a73e5929c450674da840e0cb6c21eaae8" :answer-field/choices ["q-34381/selection/b06cbb25313ebba12f59ebfc0e0cee6a6f5103f0607de43b037ce874e0096f5d" "q-34381/selection/0606c6f872a15cbcd8483d92c48658e5ff65191398a20929bb976b05389a3be5" "q-34381/selection/eb7fdef173dcb29d0b64e26e7f4a0ccc2896fd053835d1349f6a047afc188505" "q-34381/selection/bbdb8bf102d7eb5d16d4f748a0670b7a73e5929c450674da840e0cb6c21eaae8" "q-34381/selection/90622d15656212878faedabd373eccc5d61aa366798c9308a65b9883426dc53e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-34381" :question/id #uuid "556293fc-3c7f-5f32-bc07-48e166851c18" :question/math-academy-id "q-34381" :question/problem "What is the curvature of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},{t}^{3}⟩$, for $t>0?$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩=⟨2t,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(3{t}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =t\\sqrt{4+9{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that since $t>0$, we have $|t|=t.$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩=⟨2,6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨2t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,0⟩\\times ⟨2,\\,6t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}2t & 3{t}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 6t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=6{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{t}^{2}}{(t\\sqrt{4+9{t}^{2}})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{t}^{2}}{{t}^{3}(4+9{t}^{2})^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{t(4+9{t}^{2})^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-34381/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca07aabe-9fdd-5f28-b39f-1971c3591f86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132067/selection/e4cc14e7ee2a23a65270155aa145598731c0dc8a4fda6f7adb700cd83d3d5732" :answer/id #uuid "3436a242-fc1d-5700-bc0b-78658948856f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{{t}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132067/selection/b6f0bf75b50966e73eeb73054e6b83213ad28a14cbd6491c83fffa07aa98c083" :answer/id #uuid "a0f314e2-a7dc-54cb-afa6-0562c9488e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{t}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132067/selection/d2dc5f85334279b2ab3d142cf2f257ac9be9b9075ba30612233e13d82e7186b0" :answer/id #uuid "c56577ee-d483-54ed-b604-c48c5588da0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132067/selection/3a2c9fb2092e7cf954f17564bd502291723e4a0909fa45318b5babb068958e30" :answer/id #uuid "0cac0dff-665c-548e-b3f9-48d218f1a7ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132067/selection/ab3849ec97e85ce4fce51c551b2de4749ce0df6ee513890cbae83feb4c696717" :answer/id #uuid "8137a203-e5e1-5af1-ab88-eaf966f2b693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{t}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132067/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3449f4f3-aafd-5ac2-8d55-93ff5d0b8773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132067/selection/3a2c9fb2092e7cf954f17564bd502291723e4a0909fa45318b5babb068958e30" :answer-field/choices ["q-132067/selection/e4cc14e7ee2a23a65270155aa145598731c0dc8a4fda6f7adb700cd83d3d5732" "q-132067/selection/b6f0bf75b50966e73eeb73054e6b83213ad28a14cbd6491c83fffa07aa98c083" "q-132067/selection/d2dc5f85334279b2ab3d142cf2f257ac9be9b9075ba30612233e13d82e7186b0" "q-132067/selection/3a2c9fb2092e7cf954f17564bd502291723e4a0909fa45318b5babb068958e30" "q-132067/selection/ab3849ec97e85ce4fce51c551b2de4749ce0df6ee513890cbae83feb4c696717"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132067" :question/id #uuid "a6b9412b-65ef-57cc-92ea-d6766fc6fcf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-132067" :question/problem "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 0 \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)]k \\\\  & =[2{cos}^{2}⁡t-3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{sin}^{2}⁡t+3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t]k \\\\  & =(2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+{t}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t))k \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+2)k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖={t}^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{{(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132067/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca07aabe-9fdd-5f28-b39f-1971c3591f86"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132067"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34202"] :question/problem "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ at the point where $t=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩=⟨2,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩=⟨0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi )$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =⟨2,\\,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-2\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{2}{{2}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12591"] :question/problem "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t, -2t, t^2 \\rangle$ at the point where $t = 1.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the curvature $\\kappa (t),$ we will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\times \\mathbf r''(t) \\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^3}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t),$ $\\mathbf r'(1),$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(1)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨1,-2,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find $\\mathbf r''(t)$ and $\\mathbf r''(1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2),2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,2⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(1) & =⟨0,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-4\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(1){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{{3}^{3}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12608"] :question/problem "Given the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle t^2, \\: 2t, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle$, use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature of this curve as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $\\kappa (t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\times \\mathbf r''(t) \\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^3} .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({t}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the second derivative $\\mathbf{r}''(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0)⟩=⟨2,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the cross-product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨2t,2,0⟩\\times ⟨2,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2t & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2t & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2t & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the magnitude of the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{4}{8({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}=\\frac{1}{2({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12592"] :question/problem "Using the cross product formula for curvature, find the curvature of $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 2t, 1+t^2\\rangle$ as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the curvature $\\kappa (t),$ we will use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\times \\mathbf r''(t) \\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^3}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩=⟨0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $\\mathbf r''(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨2,\\,2t,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2t & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2t \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\times \\mathbf r''(t) \\| = 4,\n$$\n\nand therefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{4}{{(2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}})}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{2{(1+{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
